# Caddy in front of the HotHandZ room server.
#
# This exists for one reason: the game is served over HTTPS, and a secure page
# is not allowed to open an insecure WebSocket. The client therefore has to
# reach the server at wss://, which needs a real certificate on a real
# hostname -- you cannot get one for a bare IP address. Caddy obtains and
# renews that certificate on its own, which is the whole job.
#
# Replace the hostname, then:
#   sudo caddy fmt --overwrite /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#   sudo systemctl reload caddy
#
# Caddy upgrades WebSocket connections through reverse_proxy without any extra
# configuration, so the socket path needs no special case here. rooms.mjs
# ignores every path except /hca-ws and answers anything else with a one-line
# health message, which doubles as a way to check the box is alive from a
# browser.

rooms.example.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8787
}
